(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #116 - an untyped `Set` on a fresh name declares and
 type-locks it (docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #95), exactly like a typed declaration
 would; a later `Set` of a different type is rejected at compile time
 with the same diagnostic a typed declaration gives, rather than silently
 storing the new value's raw bits over the old type and printing an
 address. This was already the compiler's behaviour by the time #115 was
 fixed - pinned here so it cannot regress.)

Set zoo to 5.
Set zoo to "text now".
Print zoo.
